+2. **Point-Normal Form:** A unit normal vector $\mathbf{n} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ and a point $\mathbf{r} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ lying on the plane [S6]. The offset is derived as $h = -\mathbf{r} \cdot \mathbf{n}$ [G].
 
 **Formulas:**
